  "walkthroughCaddyAddressTitle": "YOUR HTTPS ADDRESS",
  "walkthroughCaddyAddressPoco": "First, the server finds its public IP address and turns it into an HTTPS address using sslip.io. PocketCoder saves that address so the mobile app knows where to sign in.",
  "walkthroughCaddyAddressChipIpAddress": "WHAT IS AN IP ADDRESS?",
  "walkthroughCaddyAddressChipHttps": "WHAT IS HTTPS?",
  "walkthroughCaddyAddressChipSslip": "WHAT IS SSLIP.IO?",
  "walkthroughCaddyWebEntryTitle": "THE SECURE WEB ENTRY",
  "walkthroughCaddyWebEntryPoco": "Caddy runs directly on the server. It sends regular web traffic to HTTPS, shares PocketCoder’s deployment status, and passes app requests to PocketBase without exposing PocketBase’s own port.",
  "walkthroughCaddyWebEntryChipCaddy": "WHAT IS CADDY?",
  "walkthroughCaddyWebEntryChipPrivatePort": "WHY IS POCKETBASE'S PORT PRIVATE?",
  "walkthroughNixosStorageTitle": "YOUR SERVER DISK",
  "walkthroughNixosStoragePoco": "This tells NixOS where PocketCoder’s main disk is and lets it expand to use the full size of the server you chose. Without autoResize, it could stay stuck at the smaller size of its original image.",
  "walkthroughNixosNetworkTitle": "NETWORK BOUNDARIES",
  "walkthroughNixosNetworkPoco": "These rules open the three standard entry ports to your server: HTTP and HTTPS for the PocketCoder website, and SSH for secure remote access. Since PocketCoder runs inside Docker, it needs its own specific rules without opening extra entry ports to the internet.",
  "walkthroughNixosNetworkChipPorts": "WHAT ARE HTTP, HTTPS, AND SSH?",
  "walkthroughNixosNetworkChipDockerRules": "WHY DOES DOCKER NEED ITS OWN RULES?",
  "walkthroughNixosNetworkChipIpVersions": "WHAT ARE IPv4 AND IPv6?",
  "walkthroughNixosSshTitle": "KEY-ONLY SSH",
  "walkthroughNixosSshPoco": "SSH is the secure way to administer a server from another device—even a phone. We accept only your SSH key—not passwords—and temporarily block repeated failed attempts.",
  "walkthroughNixosDockerTitle": "DOCKER",
  "walkthroughNixosDockerPoco": "This turns on Docker, the system that runs PocketCoder’s containers. It sends their logs to NixOS’s built-in system log, so there is one place to check what happened.",
  "walkthroughServerKeyTitle": "YOUR SERVER KEY",
  "walkthroughServerKeyPoco": "Before PocketCoder starts, this installs your public SSH key on the server. The mobile app keeps the matching private SSH key securely on your phone: the public key is the lock, and the private key is the key that opens it.",
  "walkthroughServerKeyChipPrivate": "WHAT IS A PRIVATE SSH KEY?",
  "walkthroughServerKeyChipPublic": "WHAT IS A PUBLIC SSH KEY?",
  "walkthroughServerKeyChipSsh": "WHAT IS SSH?",
  "walkthroughVerifiedVersionTitle": "VERIFIED POCKETCODER VERSION",
  "walkthroughVerifiedVersionPoco": "This downloads the exact PocketCoder version for your server, verifies it, then installs it.",
  "walkthroughVerifiedVersionChipVerification": "HOW IS THE VERSION VERIFIED?",
  "walkthroughVerifiedVersionChipDownloadFailure": "WHAT HAPPENS IF THE DOWNLOAD FAILS?",
  "walkthroughVerifiedVersionChipUpdates": "CAN I UPDATE LATER?",
  "walkthroughStartPocketCoderTitle": "START POCKETCODER",
  "walkthroughStartPocketCoderPoco": "This starts the verified PocketCoder version with only the coding harnesses you chose.",
  "walkthroughStartPocketCoderChipWhatStarts": "WHAT STARTS AFTER THIS?",
  "walkthroughStartPocketCoderChipAddHarness": "CAN I ADD A HARNESS LATER?",
  "walkthroughNixosDockerRulesTitle": "DOCKER FIREWALL RULES",
  "walkthroughNixosDockerRulesPoco": "Docker needs its own rules because it manages a separate path for container traffic. These rules keep the same boundaries without opening extra entry ports.",
  "walkthroughRuntimeSettingsTitle": "LOCAL SETTINGS",
  "walkthroughRuntimeSettingsPoco": "This prepares PocketCoder’s local settings file and locks it so only its administrator—you—can read it. It creates the internal credentials PocketCoder needs to run.",
  "walkthroughRuntimeSettingsChipLocalSettings": "WHAT ARE LOCAL SETTINGS?",
  "walkthroughRuntimeVersionTitle": "RUNNING VERSION",
  "walkthroughRuntimeVersionPoco": "PocketCoder records the version it is running in the same protected settings file.",
  "walkthroughActivationPrepareTitle": "PREPARE THE RELEASE",
  "walkthroughActivationPreparePoco": "This checks that the release files match the verified PocketCoder version and prepares them for installation. It also sets up status reporting for the PocketCoder deployment.",
  "walkthroughActivationSelectedSoftwareTitle": "SELECTED SOFTWARE",
  "walkthroughActivationSelectedSoftwarePoco": "Next, the server loads PocketCoder and only the coding agents you chose. It checks each software component before Docker runs it.",
  "walkthroughActivationSwitchTitle": "MAKE IT ACTIVE",
  "walkthroughActivationSwitchPoco": "This makes the new PocketCoder version active and starts its containers. It uses prebuilt software for faster setup and consistent versioning.",
  "walkthroughActivationHealthTitle": "CHECK THE DEPLOYMENT",
  "walkthroughActivationHealthPoco": "Before calling the deployment complete, PocketCoder checks that its core and optional services are healthy. Only then does it record this version as active.",
  "walkthroughDebianSetupStatusTitle": "SETUP STATUS",
  "walkthroughDebianSetupStatusPoco": "This setup script keeps PocketCoder’s deployment status up to date as it runs. If something fails, it records where and cleans up temporary files so it can be checked or safely retried.",
  "walkthroughDebianSetupStatusChipStatus": "HOW IS DEPLOYMENT STATUS SHOWN?",
  "walkthroughDebianSetupStatusChipFailure": "WHAT HAPPENS IF SETUP FAILS?",
  "walkthroughServicesComposeTitle": "THE DOCKER BLUEPRINT",
  "walkthroughServicesComposePoco": "Docker Compose is PocketCoder’s blueprint. It keeps your data when we update the software, and gives each component only the connections it needs.",
  "walkthroughServicesComposeChipDockerCompose": "WHAT IS DOCKER COMPOSE?",
  "walkthroughServicesComposeChipSavedData": "WHAT IS SAVED DATA?",
  "walkthroughServicesComposeChipPrivateConnections": "WHAT ARE PRIVATE CONNECTIONS?",
  "walkthroughServicesPocketBaseTitle": "POCKETBASE",
  "walkthroughServicesPocketBasePoco": "PocketBase keeps the information PocketCoder needs to run: your sign-in, skills, prompts, agent connections, and API keys. That information stays on your server, and you reach it through the HTTPS address Caddy just set up.",
  "walkthroughServicesPocketBaseChipKeeps": "WHAT DOES POCKETBASE KEEP?",
  "walkthroughServicesPocketBaseChipSignIn": "HOW DO I SIGN IN SECURELY?",
  "walkthroughServicesPocketBaseChipUpdates": "WHAT HAPPENS WHEN POCKETCODER UPDATES?",
  "walkthroughServicesHarnessesTitle": "CODING HARNESSES",
  "walkthroughServicesHarnessesPoco": "PocketCoder prepares the coding harnesses you selected: {selectedHarnesses}. Each gets its own container, saved workspace, and only the private connections it needs.",
